"{\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"For an Aeroplan award, I’d investigate the Hong Kong connection first: it gives the earliest Bangkok arrival among these late-departure options, with a shorter elapsed trip than the Taiwan alternatives. If arriving earlier in the day matters more, the Taiwan routing is a distinct tradeoff.\"},{\"k\":\"p\",\"r\":\"J1@2027-01-15T23:15-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T10:35\",\"n\":\"Hong Kong connection\",\"v\":\"This economy award via HKG arrives 35 minutes before the later Taiwan option and has a 105-minute award connection. The downside is a stop, and its 65,000 Aeroplan points plus observed CAD 107.40 fees (quote scope unknown) do not establish an all-in price.\"},{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J7@2027-01-15T12:00-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T01:25\",\"n\":\"Earlier Taiwan arrival\",\"v\":\"Choose this if reaching Bangkok earlier is the priority: it arrives 9 hours 10 minutes before the Hong Kong award above. It also has the longer elapsed journey, a 270-minute connection in TPE, and only one reported seat versus two on the Hong Kong option. Same program and points, but observed fees are CAD 116.50 with unknown scope.\"},{\"k\":\"b\",\"r\":\"C1@2027-01-15T09:40-08:00/SFO>BKK\",\"n\":\"Cash baseline\",\"v\":\"The returned Singapore Airlines cash itinerary is USD 440, with price scope unknown; it is a one-stop routing via SIN, not a like-for-like all-in comparison with an award.\"},{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"The award results are assembled itineraries, not confirmed bookings. The points and fee quote scopes are unknown, and award cabin labels do not verify every leg’s cabin. The cash quote’s scope is also unknown; the search returned one traveler, which does not make its amount a per-person fare. Results may not be real-time, and provider coverage was partial, so confirm current availability and prices before booking.\"}]}"
